 protect your endpoint with HTTP Basic Auth by specifying `basicAuth`,","+which references K8s secrets holding the username and password. `authSecret` and `basicAuth`","+are mutually exclusive, only one of them can be configured for a given endpoint.","+","+Firstly, create k8s secrets containing your username and password.","+","+```sh","+kubectl create secret generic my-webhook-basic-auth --from-literal=username=my-username --from-literal=password=my-password","+```","+","+Then add `basicAuth` to your `webhook` EventSource.","+","+```yaml","+apiVersion: argoproj.io/v1alpha1","+kind: EventSource","+metadata:","+  name: webhook","+spec:","+  webhook:","+    example:","+      port: \"12000\"","+      endpoint: /example","+      method: POST","+      basicAuth:","+        username:","+          name: my-webhook-basic-auth","+          key: username","+        password:","+          name: my-webhook-basic-auth","+          key: password","+```","+","+Now you can authenticate your webhook endpoint with the configured credentials.","+","+```sh","+curl -X POST -u my-username:my-password -d \"{your data}\" http://xxxxx:12000/example","+```"],"additions":40,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"pkg/apis/events/openapi/openapi_generated.go","lines":["@@ -8783,12 +8783,18 @@ func schema_pkg_apis_events_v1alpha1_WebhookContext(ref common.ReferenceCallback"," \t\t\t\t\t\t\tFormat:      \"int64\","," \t\t\t\t\t\t},"," \t\t\t\t\t},","+\t\t\t\t\t\"basicAuth\": {","+\t\t\t\t\t\tSchemaProps: spec.SchemaProps{","+\t\t\t\t\t\t\tDescription: \"BasicAuth holds the username and password secret selectors for basic authentication\",","+\t\t\t\t\t\t\tRef:         ref(\"github.com/argoproj/argo-events/pkg/apis/events/v1alpha1.BasicAuth\"),","+\t\t\t\t\t\t},","+\t\t\t\t\t},"," \t\t\t\t},"," \t\t\t\tRequired: []string{\"endpoint\", \"method\", \"port\", \"url\"},"," \t\t\t},"," \t\t},"," \t\tDependencies: []string{","-\t\t\t\"k8s.io/api/core/v1.SecretKeySelector\"},","+\t\t\t\"github.com/ar